# Build artifacts never belong in the image context (the Dockerfile runs its own
# clean `npm ci`). Excluding nested node_modules also stops iCloud/Finder " 2"
# duplicate dirs from poisoning the TypeScript @types auto-include.
**/node_modules
**/.next

# iCloud/Finder CONFLICT COPIES — `approvals.test 2.ts`, `build-graph 2.ts`,
# `_os-ui-env 2.tpl`. They are never tracked by git, but `docker build` copies the
# WORKING TREE, and `next build` type-checks `*.test 2.ts` because tsconfig only
# excludes `**/*.test.ts` — so a stray duplicate fails the production image build with
# errors in a file nobody edited. This is the build context's half of the fix;
# `os-ui/scripts/gate.sh` fails locally and in CI if any such file exists at all.
**/* 2.*

# Python bytecode from running the images/ test suites locally. Nothing in any image
# consumes it and a stale .pyc for a deleted module is worse than useless.
**/__pycache__

# Large directories not consumed by any Dockerfile — trim the build context.
# The os-ui Dockerfile (images/os-ui/Dockerfile) COPYs os-ui/ and docs/components
# so those are kept. Everything below is excluded.
deploy/
charts/
images/
seed/
tests/
ee/
cli/
licenses/

# Binary and generated files that bloat the context
*.sql
*.png
*.pdf
sbom.cdx.json
.git
